    "body": "Review findings fixed in 9a095b7: each facet is read as a slab thickened by an upper-bound chord sag ((h/2)·tan(θ/2) from its edge neighbours; >45° counts as a real edge, so box faces and hex flats stay exact) - a stepped bar's d40 section reads at or outside its true round (was 4.283 vs 4.444), an off-axis cylinder 20 (was 19.848); the per-line entry also reads the part's facets, so a part poking out of a box face bounds the along-line rapids (the approach used to stop inside it); round-bar bit-identity verified against #118's head (same fingerprints); refusal text and module placement fixed; shank-branch test. Unwelded-mesh gap -> #121. Suites green, clippy clean. Merges after the v0.13.0 tag, after #118.",
